  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry you've lost your connection. Since you're working from home, the problem is probably either your home network or the laptop's Wi-Fi. Please try these steps in order and check after each one whether websites load:\n\n1. Do your phone or other devices on the same Wi-Fi get online? If none of them do, the problem is your home internet, not the laptop.\n2. On the laptop, turn Wi-Fi off and back on. If that doesn't help, forget the network and reconnect.\n3. Restart the laptop.\n4. Restart your home router: unplug it for about 30 seconds, plug it back in, and wait a few minutes for it to come back up.\n5. If it's still not working, connect the laptop to your phone's hotspot or plug in a network cable. This tells us whether the laptop itself is the problem.\n\nPlease reply and tell us whether your other devices work and which step, if any, fixed it. Once you're back online, please leave the laptop on and signed in for about 30 minutes. Our records show it hasn't checked in with our management system for a while, and this gives it time to catch up on updates. If none of the steps work, let us know and we'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "User: Sofia Rossi (id 7), account active, VPN access true, no lockout or block. Device BL-LT-0107 is showing offline. Last check-in was 2026-09-27, with the warning 'No check-in for 12 days'. Being offline fits the no-internet report (KB-014 quick check 3). But the 12-day gap is longer than an outage that started today. Either the laptop has been off or disconnected for a while, or the problem is older than reported. That makes this a KB-018 follow-up as well (more than 7 days without check-in). Sent the user the KB-014 steps: check other devices, toggle Wi-Fi or forget and rejoin the network, restart the laptop, restart the router, try a hotspot or cable. Also asked her to stay online for 30 minutes once connected so the device can check in. Next: re-run check_device_status after she replies. Escalate under KB-018 if the device comes online but still doesn't check in, or if the laptop can't connect even on a hotspot or cable (possible hardware or driver fault).",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014",
    "KB-018"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
